The most recent Mercedes-Benz S-Class S65 is the W222 generation (2014-2019). It is powered by a 6.0L twin-turbocharged V12 engine. I will evaluate based on the specifications and characteristics of the W222 S65 AMG, comparing it to today's market benchmarks.

- **price_usd**: The W222 S65 AMG was a top-tier model with a very high price when new, around $230,000 - $265,000. Used prices average around $81,068, but new prices were significantly above the market average of $52,000. Score: -1.00.
- **total_cost_estimate_5yr_usd**: As a V12 AMG S-Class, this car has very high depreciation, insurance, maintenance, and potential repair costs. Maintenance can easily cost $3,000-$5,000 per year or more, especially with the complex suspension and V12 engine. Repair costs can be substantial. This will likely exceed $80,000 over 5 years. Score: -1.00.
- **insurance_usd_yr**: A high-performance V12 luxury sedan is in the highest insurance groups (Group 44-50 in the UK). This indicates very high insurance costs. Score: -1.00.
- **maint_usd_yr**: Maintenance for a V12 S-Class is extremely expensive due to parts cost, specialized labor, and the complexity of the engine and systems. Spark plug changes are more frequent and costly than on V8s. Score: -1.00.
